1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:03,400
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,319
I'm Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

3
00:00:05,319 --> 00:00:06,960
This is my little brother,
George.

4
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:08,080
[SNORTS]

5
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:10,280
This is Mommy Pig.
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:12,799
And this is Daddy Pig.
[GRUNTS]

7
00:00:12,799 --> 00:00:14,240
[ALL LAUGH]

8
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:15,760
Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

9
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,919
[♪♪♪]

10
00:00:17,919 --> 00:00:20,119
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

11
00:00:20,119 --> 00:00:22,200
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

12
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,279
[PEPPA AND GEORGE SLURPING]

13
00:00:26,279 --> 00:00:28,919
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George
are drinking orange juice.

14
00:00:28,919 --> 00:00:31,000
[SLURPING]

15
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,600
[SNORTS]
What noisy little piggies!

16
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,720
[BOTH LAUGH]

17
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:38,559
George, look at all
the tiny bubbles.

18
00:00:38,559 --> 00:00:40,760
[GRUNTS]
[GIGGLES]

19
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:42,919
I can make
bigger bubbles.

20
00:00:42,919 --> 00:00:45,480
[INHALES]
[BUBBLES GURGLING]

21
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:47,839
NARRATOR:
Peppa is blowing bubbles
in her drink.

22
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:49,360
Hee-hee-hee! 
Bub-ble!

23
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:51,559
NARRATOR:
George wants
to blow bubbles too.

24
00:00:51,559 --> 00:00:52,760
[INHALES]

25
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,199
[BUBBLES GURGLE]
[LAUGHS]

26
00:00:54,199 --> 00:00:56,559
[GURGLING CONTINUES]

27
00:00:56,559 --> 00:01:00,680
Peppa, George, you really
shouldn't play with your food.

28
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:02,239
Sorry, Daddy.
[GRUNTS]

29
00:01:02,239 --> 00:01:04,200
Peppa, if you
like bubbles,

30
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:06,480
why don't you play with
your bubble mixture?

31
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:08,679
Yes! My bubble mixture!

32
00:01:08,679 --> 00:01:10,119
[GRUNTS]
George!

33
00:01:10,119 --> 00:01:12,759
Let's blow bubbles
in the garden.
[GRUNTS]

34
00:01:12,759 --> 00:01:15,640
[BOTH LAUGH]

35
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:18,479
NARRATOR:
Peppa is showing George
how to blow bubbles.

36
00:01:18,479 --> 00:01:21,839
First, dip the stick
in the mixture.

37
00:01:21,839 --> 00:01:23,160
[♪♪♪]

38
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:26,800
Then, take a big breath...
and blow.

39
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:29,000
[INHALES, BLOWS]

40
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,720
[LAUGHS]

41
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:32,800
Bub-ble!
[POP]

42
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:34,679
[BOTH GIGGLING]

43
00:01:34,679 --> 00:01:38,000
George, now it's your turn.
[GRUNTS]

44
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,440
Dip the stick
in the mixture.

45
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:43,320
Hold it up.

46
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:45,600
Take a big breath...
[INHALES]

47
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:47,280
...and blow.

48
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,960
[BLOWING]

49
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,880
NARRATOR:
George is trying really hard,

50
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:53,800
but he is running out
of breath.

51
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:55,839
[POP]
Achoo!

52
00:01:55,839 --> 00:01:57,679
[BOTH GIGGLE]

53
00:01:57,679 --> 00:02:00,479
George, you didn't blow
hard enough.

54
00:02:00,479 --> 00:02:02,360
[♪♪♪]

55
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:04,880
I know a way George
can make bubbles.

56
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:07,600
Dip the stick
in the mixture...

57
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:11,280
then lift it up
and wave it around.

58
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,760
[GIGGLES, SNORTS]

59
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:14,400
Bub-ble!

60
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:16,840
[ALL LAUGHING]

61
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:19,640
[SNORTS]
It's even better
if you run along.

62
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:21,160
[GRUNTS]

63
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:24,000
[LAUGHS]

64
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,600
Wait for me.

65
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:29,519
NARRATOR:
George is having fun
making bubbles...

66
00:02:29,519 --> 00:02:31,120
[SNORTING]
[GIGGLING]

67
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:33,519
NARRATOR:
and Peppa is having fun
popping them.

68
00:02:33,519 --> 00:02:36,560
I love bubbles.
[SNORTS]

69
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:38,320
[GIGGLES]
[GRUNTS]

70
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:41,680
NARRATOR:
Oh, dear, the bubble mixture
is all used up.

71
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:43,160
[CRYING]

72
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:45,239
Daddy, Mommy!

73
00:02:45,239 --> 00:02:48,120
[GRUNTS]
There's no more
bubble mixture.

74
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:50,959
Don't worry, Peppa,
I have an idea.

75
00:02:50,959 --> 00:02:52,400
[SNORTS]
Mommy Pig!

76
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:54,560
Bring me
a bucket please.

77
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:56,600
Yes, Daddy Pig.

78
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,679
Peppa.
Bring me some soap.

79
00:02:58,679 --> 00:03:00,440
Yes, Daddy Pig.

80
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:03,640
George, bring me
my old tennis racquet.

81
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:05,200
[GRUNTS]

82
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:08,959
NARRATOR:
A bucket? Some soap?
A tennis racquet?

83
00:03:08,959 --> 00:03:11,359
What is Daddy Pig doing?

84
00:03:11,359 --> 00:03:13,880
First,
I need some water.

85
00:03:14,519 --> 00:03:17,000
[SPIGOT SQUEAKS]

86
00:03:18,239 --> 00:03:19,480
Then the soap.

87
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:21,560
[GIGGLING]

88
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:24,000
And now,
the tennis racquet, please.

89
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,720
[SNORTS]
Thank you.

90
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:27,920
Now watch this.

91
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:31,560
[INHALES, BLOWS]

92
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:33,959
[BUBBLE SNAPS]
ALL: Ooh! Wow!

93
00:03:33,959 --> 00:03:35,600
[GIGGLING]

94
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:38,519
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig has made
his own bubble mixture.

95
00:03:39,959 --> 00:03:41,880
Come on, everyone.

96
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,200
[LAUGHING]

97
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:45,560
Be careful, Daddy Pig,
don't slip and fall.

98
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:47,720
[SNORTS]
I'll be fine.

99
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:49,799
Whoa! Oof!

100
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:53,760
Ah! Oof!

101
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:58,399
Are you okay,
Daddy Pig?

102
00:03:58,399 --> 00:04:01,839
Yes, I'm fine.
Achoo!

103
00:04:01,839 --> 00:04:03,519
ALL:
Wow!

104
00:04:03,519 --> 00:04:06,200
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig has made
the biggest bubble ever.

105
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:07,560
[POPPING]

106
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:09,519
[ALL LAUGHING]

107
00:04:09,519 --> 00:04:12,880
Oh dear, I've spilt
all my bubble mixture.

108
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:15,679
Now we can't make
any more bubbles.

109
00:04:15,679 --> 00:04:17,079
Hm.

110
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:19,039
[SNORTS]
But we can play

111
00:04:19,039 --> 00:04:21,360
jumping in
muddy puddles. Look!

112
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:24,479
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig's bubble mixture
has made a big, muddy puddle.

113
00:04:24,479 --> 00:04:26,120
ALL:
Hooray!

114
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:27,880
[SLOSHING]

115
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:31,599
NARRATOR:
Peppa loves jumping up
and down in muddy puddles.

116
00:04:31,599 --> 00:04:35,640
Look! The bubble mixture
has made the puddle all bubbly.

117
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:37,120
[GIGGLES]

118
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:39,159
NARRATOR:
Peppa loves
jumping up and down

119
00:04:39,159 --> 00:04:40,919
in muddy, bubbly puddles.

120
00:04:40,919 --> 00:04:44,159
Everyone loves jumping up and
down in muddy, bubbly puddles.

121
00:04:44,159 --> 00:04:45,919
[ALL LAUGHING]

122
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:48,640
[SCHOOL BELL RINGING]

123
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:49,960
[♪♪♪]

124
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:52,599
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

125
00:04:52,599 --> 00:04:54,479
[ALL LAUGHING]

126
00:04:54,479 --> 00:04:58,919
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her friends
are going to playgroup today.

127
00:04:58,919 --> 00:05:00,880
The children each have
their own hook

128
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:02,120
to hang their coats on.

129
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:04,560
[ALL CONTINUE LAUGHING]

130
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:09,599
Today we have a new pupil,
Emily Elephant.

131
00:05:09,599 --> 00:05:10,880
KIDS:
Hello, Emily!

132
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,000
Hello.

133
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,120
NARRATOR:
Emily is a bit shy.

134
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:17,320
MADAME GAZELLE:
Who would like to show Emily
where to hang her coat?

135
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:19,440
ALL:
Me! Me! Me! Me!

136
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:22,120
Ho, ho,
we just need one.

137
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:25,840
Peppa, can you show Emily
where to hang her coat?

138
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:27,599
Yes, Madame Gazelle.

139
00:05:27,599 --> 00:05:31,120
[GRUNTS]
We each have
our own coat hooks.

140
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:33,719
This one is for
you, Emily.

141
00:05:33,719 --> 00:05:37,479
NARRATOR:
Emily is hanging her coat
on her very own coat hook.

142
00:05:37,479 --> 00:05:40,560
Now Emily, what would
you like to do today?

143
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:44,200
Painting, clay
or building blocks?

144
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:49,760
Um... I don't know.
Maybe building blocks.

145
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:53,919
MADAME GAZELLE:
And everyone else, painting,
clay or building blocks?

146
00:05:53,919 --> 00:05:55,520
ALL:
Building blocks!

147
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:57,880
[ALL LAUGHING]

148
00:05:57,880 --> 00:05:59,159
My goodness!

149
00:05:59,159 --> 00:06:01,560
Building blocks
are popular today!

150
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:04,159
NARRATOR:
Everyone wants to sit
next to Emily Elephant.

151
00:06:04,159 --> 00:06:05,400
[SNORTS]
Emily,

152
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:08,320
you put one block
on top of another.

153
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:09,840
Like this.

154
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:13,159
Woof! Woof! It's better if
you put them side by side.

155
00:06:13,159 --> 00:06:16,280
Baaa!
No, this way, Emily.

156
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:19,080
Meow! This is
the right way, Emily.

157
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:22,599
Neigh! No, Emily!
Like this.

158
00:06:22,599 --> 00:06:24,919
You're all being
very helpful.

159
00:06:24,919 --> 00:06:28,479
But Emily, how would you play
with the blocks?

160
00:06:28,479 --> 00:06:33,560
Um... I'm not very sure.
I might do it like this.

161
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:37,359
ALL:
Wow!

162
00:06:37,359 --> 00:06:39,919
NARRATOR:
Emily Elephant is good
at building blocks.

163
00:06:39,919 --> 00:06:41,039
[RINGING]

164
00:06:41,039 --> 00:06:42,359
NARRATOR:
It is playtime.

165
00:06:42,359 --> 00:06:46,320
ALL:
Hooray! Ha-ha-ha-ha!

166
00:06:46,320 --> 00:06:49,919
Emily, would you like to play
outside with the others?

167
00:06:49,919 --> 00:06:51,359
Yes, please.

168
00:06:51,359 --> 00:06:53,840
Can someone show Emily
where we play?

169
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:55,039
[KIDS LAUGH]

170
00:06:55,039 --> 00:06:56,799
[GRUNTS]
Yes, Madame Gazelle.

171
00:06:56,799 --> 00:06:58,320
[KIDS LAUGH]

172
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,680
NARRATOR:
At playtime,
Peppa and her friends

173
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:02,719
play in the school garden.

174
00:07:02,719 --> 00:07:04,599
DANNY:
Woof! Woof!
Can't catch me!

175
00:07:04,599 --> 00:07:07,280
[ALL SHOUTING]
NARRATOR: What a lot of noise!

176
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:10,400
Let's see who is
the loudest.

177
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:12,479
Okay. I'll go first.

178
00:07:12,479 --> 00:07:15,000
[INHALES]
Squeak! Squeak!

179
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,680
NARRATOR:
That was quite loud.

180
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,320
Now it is Zoë Zebra's turn.

181
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:21,120
[INHALES, SNORTS]

182
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,440
NARRATOR:
Now Suzy Sheep.

183
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:23,520
Baa-baa!

184
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:24,840
NARRATOR:
Now Danny Dog.

185
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:26,120
Woof! Woof!

186
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:27,560
NARRATOR:
That was very loud.

187
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:29,680
My turn! Meow!

188
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:31,520
My turn! Neigh!

189
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:32,719
My turn!

190
00:07:32,719 --> 00:07:33,880
[SNORTS]

191
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:35,440
NARRATOR:
Peppa is the loudest.

192
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:38,359
[KIDS LAUGH]

193
00:07:38,359 --> 00:07:40,120
Emily, you try!

194
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:41,840
I'm not too sure.

195
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:44,039
ALL:
Please, Emily!

196
00:07:44,039 --> 00:07:46,680
Okay. I'll try.

197
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:48,000
[INHALES]

198
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,880
[TRUMPETS]

199
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:52,760
NARRATOR:
My goodness! That was loud.

200
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:54,520
KIDS:
Wow!

201
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:56,440
[GRUNTS]
Do it again!

202
00:07:56,440 --> 00:07:57,760
[INHALES]

203
00:07:57,760 --> 00:07:59,880
[TRUMPETS]

204
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:01,120
[ALL LAUGH]

205
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,359
[GIGGLING]

206
00:08:02,359 --> 00:08:05,919
NARRATOR:
Emily is not shy anymore.

207
00:08:05,919 --> 00:08:07,320
[GRUNTS]
Emily,

208
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:10,159
would you like to play
my favorite game?

209
00:08:10,159 --> 00:08:12,120
What is
your favorite game?

210
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:14,359
Jumping in muddy puddles!

211
00:08:14,359 --> 00:08:16,919
That's my favorite game
too!

212
00:08:16,919 --> 00:08:18,679
[SLOSHING, LAUGHING]

213
00:08:18,679 --> 00:08:21,520
NARRATOR:
Peppa loves jumping up and down
in muddy puddles.

214
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:24,280
Emily loves jumping up and down
in muddy puddles.

215
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:27,200
This looks like fun.
Yippee!

216
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:30,320
NARRATOR:
Madame Gazelle loves jumping up
and down in muddy puddles.

217
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:32,199
[ALL LAUGHING]

218
00:08:32,199 --> 00:08:35,240
NARRATOR:
Everyone loves jumping up
and down in muddy puddles.

219
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:37,799
[LAUGHING]

220
00:08:37,799 --> 00:08:41,760
Emily, have you enjoyed your
first day at our playgroup?

221
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:43,679
Yes, Madame Gazelle!

222
00:08:43,679 --> 00:08:46,360
And I see you've made
lots of new friends.

223
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,480
Yes!
Ha-ha-ha!

224
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:52,000
Emily Elephant
is my friend.

225
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,680
Baa-baa.
And Emily's my friend.

226
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:55,840
And mine.
And mine.

227
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,720
And mine.
And mine.
And mine.

228
00:08:57,720 --> 00:08:59,240
[GRUNTS]
Emily,

229
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:01,240
who do you 
like best?

230
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:05,600
Um... I like Suzy
and Danny and Zoë

231
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:09,360
and Rebecca and Pedro
and Peppa.

232
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:11,480
[ALL LAUGH]

233
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,480
[LAUGHS]

234
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:16,880
[TRUMPETS]

235
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:19,880
[♪♪♪]

236
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:22,920
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

237
00:09:22,920 --> 00:09:26,160
NARRATOR:
Granny and Grandpa Pig
are going on holiday.

238
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:28,199
They are bringing Polly Parrot
to Peppa's house,

239
00:09:28,199 --> 00:09:30,680
so Peppa and George
can look after her.

240
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:32,280
[SQUAWKS]

241
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:34,400
[HORN HONKING, BRAKES SCREECH]

242
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:37,199
[SNORTS]
Hello, everyone!

243
00:09:37,199 --> 00:09:39,000
[SNORTS]
Hello, Grandpa Pig!

244
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Hello, Granny Pig!
[GRUNTS]

245
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,880
[SNORTS]
Polly is very excited

246
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:45,040
about her holiday
with Peppa and George.

247
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:46,600
[SNORTS]
Hello, Polly.

248
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:47,800
[SQUAWKS]

249
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:49,560
Hello, Polly.
[ALL LAUGH]

250
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:54,560
NARRATOR:
Polly Parrot copies
everything that is said.

251
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:57,360
[SNORTS]
What's in Polly's suitcase,
Granny?

252
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:59,520
[SNORTS]
This is Polly's food.

253
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:03,040
George, can you guess
what Polly likes to eat best?

254
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:04,880
Chocolate
Cake!

255
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:08,319
[CHUCKLES]
No, not chocolate cake.

256
00:10:08,319 --> 00:10:09,959
Polly likes birdseed.

257
00:10:09,959 --> 00:10:11,680
[SQUAWKS]
Birdseed!

258
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:12,959
[LAUGHING]

259
00:10:12,959 --> 00:10:14,720
[GRUNTS]
Can I feed her,
Granny Pig?

260
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,839
Can I feed her?

261
00:10:15,839 --> 00:10:17,360
[SNORTS]
Yes!

262
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:21,079
It's very important not to
give Polly too much food.

263
00:10:21,079 --> 00:10:23,199
Yes, Grandpa Pig.
[SNORTS]

264
00:10:23,199 --> 00:10:25,800
Grandpa, can Polly
come out of the cage?

265
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:29,880
Yes, but you must keep all
the doors and windows closed,

266
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:32,040
so Polly
doesn't fly away.

267
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:33,680
Yes,
Grandpa Pig.

268
00:10:33,680 --> 00:10:36,520
[SNORTS]
Goodbye, Peppa.
Goodbye, George.

269
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:38,240
[SNORTS]
Goodbye, Granny Pig!

270
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:39,720
Goodbye,
Grandpa Pig!

271
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:42,120
[SQUAWKS]
Goodbye, Granny Pig!

272
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:43,800
Goodbye, Grandpa Pig!

273
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:45,920
[ALL LAUGH]

274
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:47,800
Would you like
a cup of tea?

275
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:50,680
[SQUAWKS]
Would you like
a cup of tea?

276
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:52,199
[GIGGLES]

277
00:10:52,199 --> 00:10:54,319
NARRATOR:
George has got
Polly's birdseed.

278
00:10:54,319 --> 00:10:56,800
[GIGGLING]
PEPPA: George!

279
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:58,800
That is
too much birdseed.

280
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:01,959
Polly will grow very big
and burst like a balloon.

281
00:11:01,959 --> 00:11:03,240
Pop!

282
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:04,360
[SQUAWKS]

283
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:06,600
Burst like a balloon.
Pop!

284
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,880
[ALL LAUGHING]

285
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:11,319
[ICE CREAM TRUCK TUNE PLAYS]

286
00:11:11,319 --> 00:11:13,439
[SNORTS]
What's that noise?

287
00:11:13,439 --> 00:11:15,480
Ice cream!
[SNORTS]

288
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:17,120
[LAUGHING]

289
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:18,280
[SQUAWKS]

290
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:21,640
[GRUNTS]
Ice cream, hooray!

291
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:23,680
[SNORTS]
NARRATOR: Oh dear,

292
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:25,920
George has forgotten
to close the door.

293
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:28,079
[SQUAWKS]

294
00:11:28,079 --> 00:11:30,400
[♪♪♪]

295
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:32,719
Ice cream. Ice cream!
[BELL RINGS]

296
00:11:32,719 --> 00:11:35,160
NARRATOR:
It is Miss Rabbit,
the ice cream lady.

297
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:36,319
Hello, Mommy Pig.

298
00:11:36,319 --> 00:11:37,880
[GRUNTS]
Hello, Miss Rabbit.

299
00:11:37,880 --> 00:11:39,920
Four ice creams,
please.

300
00:11:41,760 --> 00:11:43,400
Thank you,
Miss Rabbit.

301
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:44,959
[SLURPING, GIGGLING]

302
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:49,480
George!
You forgot to close the door!

303
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:52,000
[SNORTS]
Polly will have flown away!

304
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,560
[GRUNTS]
Don't worry, Peppa.

305
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:55,959
I'm sure Polly
is still inside.

306
00:11:57,959 --> 00:11:59,480
Polly's not here!

307
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:03,160
Oh.
[CRIES]

308
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:04,680
We've lost Polly.

309
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:07,959
Grandpa and Granny
are going to be very sad.

310
00:12:07,959 --> 00:12:11,480
[SNORTS]
Maybe we should try
the garden.

311
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,719
Look! What's that?

312
00:12:13,719 --> 00:12:16,120
NARRATOR:
What has Mommy Pig seen
in the garden?

313
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,920
[SQUAWKS]

314
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:19,480
PEPPA: It's Polly!
ALL: Hooray!

315
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:21,120
[SQUAWKS]

316
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:25,520
But Daddy, how are we going to
get Polly down from the tree?

317
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:26,880
[SQUAWKS]

318
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:29,719
[SNORTING]
Don't worry Peppa,
I'll rescue Polly.

319
00:12:29,719 --> 00:12:31,240
[♪♪♪]

320
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:32,520
Come on, Polly.

321
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:35,599
[SQUAWKS]
Would you like
a cup of tea?

322
00:12:35,599 --> 00:12:39,040
NARRATOR:
Oh, no, Polly has flown
higher up the tree!

323
00:12:39,040 --> 00:12:40,160
Oh, dear.

324
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:42,280
[SNORTS]
Be careful, Daddy!

325
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:45,880
Don't fall out of the tree
like you always do.

326
00:12:45,880 --> 00:12:48,920
Don't worry, Peppa,
I'll be very careful.

327
00:12:48,920 --> 00:12:51,000
[SNORTS]
Come on, Polly.

328
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,280
[SQUAWKS]
Birdseed!

329
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:54,640
[GRUNTS]

330
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:56,839
NARRATOR:
I wonder where
George is going?

331
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:01,040
George has got
Polly's birdseed.

332
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:03,160
Polly loves to eat birdseed.

333
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:05,599
[SQUAWKS]

334
00:13:05,599 --> 00:13:06,839
[LAUGHS]

335
00:13:06,839 --> 00:13:09,319
George has got Polly
down from the tree!

336
00:13:09,319 --> 00:13:10,599
ALL: Hooray!
[ALL SNORT]

337
00:13:10,599 --> 00:13:11,880
[PHONE RINGING]

338
00:13:11,880 --> 00:13:13,439
What's that noise?

339
00:13:13,439 --> 00:13:15,920
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig's mobile phone
is ringing!

340
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:19,240
What? Whoa! Oof!
[PHONE CONTINUES RINGING]

341
00:13:20,280 --> 00:13:21,959
[PHONE BEEPS]
Hello?

342
00:13:21,959 --> 00:13:23,240
Oh, Granny Pig.

343
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:25,719
Hello, Daddy Pig.

344
00:13:25,719 --> 00:13:28,400
[SNORTS]
Please, may I talk
to Polly?

345
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:30,520
Yes, of course.

346
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:34,000
GRANNY PIG:
Hello, Polly. Are you having
a nice holiday?

347
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,079
[SQUAWKS]
Hello, Polly.

348
00:13:36,079 --> 00:13:38,599
POLLY:
Are you having
a nice holiday?

349
00:13:38,599 --> 00:13:40,599
[BOTH LAUGHING, SNORTING]

350
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:43,880
[ALL LAUGHING]

351
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:51,199
[♪♪♪]

352
00:13:51,199 --> 00:13:53,120
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

353
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:58,079
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her family
are going out for the day.

354
00:13:58,079 --> 00:13:59,760
Daddy Pig has made a picnic.

355
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:01,880
[GRUNTS]
Peppa? George?

356
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:03,160
Have you got
your stuff ready?

357
00:14:03,160 --> 00:14:05,920
[GRUNTS]
Yes! I'm taking
Teddy.

358
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:07,360
Dine-Saw!

359
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:10,360
If you take your toys,
you must look after them.

360
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:12,199
Yes, Mommy.
[GRUNTS]

361
00:14:12,199 --> 00:14:14,240
[KIDS LAUGHING]

362
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:17,520
Are we all ready?

363
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:18,959
[IN UNISON]
Yes, Daddy Pig!

364
00:14:18,959 --> 00:14:21,079
Then let's go!
[STARTS ENGINE]

365
00:14:21,079 --> 00:14:22,640
Dine-Saw!
[CRYING]

366
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:25,319
NARRATOR:
George has left
Mr. Dinosaur behind.

367
00:14:25,319 --> 00:14:28,240
[CONTINUES CRYING]
Oh, George.

368
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:31,280
You should take more
care of Mr. Dinosaur.

369
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:34,479
Dine-Saw!

370
00:14:34,479 --> 00:14:38,479
Are we all absolutely sure we
haven't forgotten anything else?

371
00:14:38,479 --> 00:14:40,920
Yes, Daddy Pig!
[STARTS ENGINE]

372
00:14:40,920 --> 00:14:43,479
Teddy! I've left Teddy!
[BRAKES SCREECH]

373
00:14:43,479 --> 00:14:45,199
Where did you leave Teddy?

374
00:14:45,199 --> 00:14:48,079
I think,
on the kitchen table.

375
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:52,959
Peppa! You really must
take more care of Teddy.

376
00:14:53,839 --> 00:14:56,640
Teddy! Hee-hee!
[SNORTS]

377
00:14:56,640 --> 00:14:58,199
Here we go again.
[STARTS ENGINE]

378
00:14:58,199 --> 00:14:59,360
All Ready?

379
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:00,839
[IN UNISON]
Yes, Daddy Pig!

380
00:15:00,839 --> 00:15:02,439
Here we go!

381
00:15:02,439 --> 00:15:03,599
[HONKS HORN]

382
00:15:03,599 --> 00:15:05,719
NARRATOR:
This is the picnic area.

383
00:15:05,719 --> 00:15:06,800
We're here.

384
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:08,839
Hooray!
[KIDS GIGGLE]

385
00:15:08,839 --> 00:15:13,079
Ahh! I love this picnic spot.
[GRUNTS]

386
00:15:13,079 --> 00:15:15,680
It's so quiet and peaceful.

387
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:18,959
[MUSICAL CAR HORN PLAYS]

388
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:23,000
NARRATOR:
It is Zoë Zebra, with her
daddy, Mr. Zebra the Postman.

389
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,280
Hello, Mr. Zebra.
[GRUNTS]

390
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:27,199
Have you got our post?

391
00:15:27,199 --> 00:15:30,120
Ho, ho.
No deliveries today.

392
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:31,520
It's my day off.

393
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:34,920
[SNORTS]
Neigh! We're having
a picnic lunch.

394
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:36,439
[GRUNTS]
So are we!

395
00:15:36,439 --> 00:15:39,520
I know! Why don't we make
one big picnic?

396
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:40,839
Yes!

397
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:42,839
[ALL MUNCHING]

398
00:15:42,839 --> 00:15:45,240
NARRATOR:
What a splendid picnic!

399
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:46,439
[ALL SLURPING]

400
00:15:46,439 --> 00:15:47,760
[GRUNTS]
Please may George and I

401
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:50,240
leave the table,
and play with Zoë?

402
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:54,160
Yes, Peppa.
[KIDS GIGGLING]

403
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:56,880
[GRUNTS]
Zoe, I've got my Teddy.

404
00:15:56,880 --> 00:15:59,680
I've got my Monkey.
Ooh, ooh, ooh.

405
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:02,560
Dine-Saw!
Grrrrrrrrr!

406
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:05,880
[LAUGHS]
I've got a toy picnic set.

407
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:07,800
Let's play picnics.

408
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:09,319
[QUACKING]

409
00:16:09,319 --> 00:16:11,240
Oh, it's the ducks.

410
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:14,520
They always turn up
when we have a picnic.

411
00:16:14,520 --> 00:16:17,520
We've got pretend
orange juice.

412
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:20,359
And we've got
pretend cake.

413
00:16:20,359 --> 00:16:22,400
[KIDS LAUGH]

414
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:23,560
[QUACKING]

415
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:26,760
It's pretend cake.
It's very nice.

416
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:28,359
[DUCK QUACKS]
NARRATOR: Oh, dear.

417
00:16:28,359 --> 00:16:31,240
I do not think
the ducks want pretend cake.

418
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:34,280
Oh, well. That means
there's more for Monkey,

419
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:36,599
Mr. Dinosaur and Teddy.

420
00:16:36,599 --> 00:16:38,640
PEPPA [IMITATING TEDDY]:
Mm. Delicious!

421
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:39,760
Ooh, ooh, ooh.

422
00:16:39,760 --> 00:16:42,920
Monkey says,
“The best cake ever!"

423
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:44,560
[ALL LAUGH]

424
00:16:44,560 --> 00:16:47,760
MOMMY PIG:
Peppa, George! Home time!

425
00:16:47,760 --> 00:16:50,400
Bye bye, Zoë!
Bye bye!

426
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:52,160
Are we all ready?

427
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:55,439
Yes, Daddy Pig!
[HONKS HORN]

428
00:16:55,439 --> 00:16:58,160
Home time for us
too, Zoë.

429
00:16:58,160 --> 00:16:59,959
Yes, Daddy.

430
00:16:59,959 --> 00:17:03,800
Cups, plates,
Monkey, Teddy...

431
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:06,919
Oh, no! You shouldn't
be here, Teddy!

432
00:17:06,919 --> 00:17:10,399
NARRATOR:
Peppa has forgotten her Teddy.
Again!

433
00:17:10,399 --> 00:17:11,639
[HORN HONKS]

434
00:17:11,639 --> 00:17:13,599
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her family are home.

435
00:17:13,599 --> 00:17:16,800
Ahh! That's enough driving
for one day.

436
00:17:16,800 --> 00:17:18,960
All I want to do now
is relax,

437
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:20,680
put my feet up
and watch some--

438
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:23,159
Teddy!
I forgot Teddy!

439
00:17:23,159 --> 00:17:26,079
Oh, Peppa! Now Daddy Pig
will have to drive

440
00:17:26,079 --> 00:17:28,280
all the way back
to the picnic spot.

441
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:30,680
Uh... Yes, of course.

442
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:33,040
[MUSICAL CAR HORN PLAYS]

443
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:35,520
It's Mr. Zebra, the Postman!

444
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:38,520
I thought it was your
day off today, Mr. Zebra.

445
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:40,360
It is my day off.

446
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:43,360
But Zoë's got
a very special delivery

447
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:45,720
for a Miss Peppa Pig.

448
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:47,159
Here you are, Peppa.

449
00:17:47,159 --> 00:17:49,120
What is it?

450
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:50,520
It's Teddy!

451
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:54,919
You left Teddy behind,
so we brought him home.

452
00:17:54,919 --> 00:17:56,440
Thank you, Zoë!

453
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:59,280
Teddy certainly has had
an exciting day out.

454
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:03,000
But Peppa, you really must
take better care of him.

455
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:07,320
Yes, Mommy. You are
a very naughty Teddy.

456
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:12,159
You must promise
not to wander off ever again.

457
00:18:12,159 --> 00:18:15,360
[IMITATING TEDDY]
Sorry, Peppa. I promise.

458
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:18,760
[ALL LAUGHING,
GRUNTING, SNORTING]

459
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:20,080
[♪♪♪]

460
00:18:20,080 --> 00:18:21,040
[GRUNTING]

461
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:23,680
PEPPA:
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

462
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:25,639
[GIGGLING, SNORTING]

463
00:18:25,639 --> 00:18:27,760
KIDS:
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

464
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:29,000
[SNORTING, GRUNTING]

465
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,120
[GIGGLING]

466
00:18:30,120 --> 00:18:31,600
KIDS:
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

467
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:34,240
[GRUNTS]

